<template>
  <main class="legal wrap">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 10 November 2026</p>
    <p>By using the Minecraft Title Generator, you agree that you have read and agree to this policy.</p>
    <p>This policy describes what data the title generator stores, why, how long it is kept, and how to remove it.</p>

    <h2>Definitions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>"I", "me", and "my" refer to Ewan Howell, who makes and runs the title generator.</li>
      <li>"You" and "your" refer to anyone using the title generator.</li>
      <li>"The title generator" refers to the Minecraft Title Generator: the website at <a href="https://mctitlegenerator.com">mctitlegenerator.com</a>, and the <a href="https://www.blockbench.net/plugins/minecraft_title_generator" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Minecraft Title Generator plugin for Blockbench</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>I may update this policy at any time. Any changes will be made on this page, and the date at the top will be updated. Changes are effective from that date.</p>

    <h2>Making titles</h2>
    <p>Titles are made in your browser, or in Blockbench when you use the plugin. They only reach my server if you save them to your account or share them.</p>
    <p>A share link holds the title's settings in the link itself. My server reads them when the link is opened, but does not store them. When a link preview is shown, eg on Discord, a preview image is made from the link and cached.</p>
    <p>Images and fonts you add yourself stay on your device, and are never included in share links or presets.</p>

    <h2>Signing in</h2>
    <p>Signing in is optional. You can sign in with Discord or GitHub to keep your presets under your account, share presets under your name, and send submissions. Signing in works the same on the website and in the Blockbench plugin.</p>
    <p>When you sign in, I only keep your account id, username, email address and a link to your profile picture from Discord or GitHub. Nothing else from your profile is stored. The access Discord or GitHub gives the title generator is only used once to read your profile, and is not kept.</p>
    <p>These are kept in a cookie on your device, or in Blockbench's storage when you use the plugin, so you stay signed in. Your profile picture is shown while you are signed in, and is loaded straight from Discord or GitHub. Your account id and username are only saved on my server once you save a preset to your account, share a preset while signed in, or send a submission. Your email address is only saved on my server while you have a submission waiting for review, or while you are a reviewer. Your profile picture link is never saved on my server. Your username and profile picture are updated each time you sign in.</p>

    <h2>Presets</h2>
    <p>When you are signed in, your saved presets are stored under your account so you can use them on any device. This stores each preset's name and title settings.</p>
    <p>Shared presets are public. Anyone can see a shared preset's name, its title and settings, when it was shared, and its downloads and rating. If you shared it while signed in, your username and whether you use Discord or GitHub are shown with it.</p>
    <p>If you share a preset without signing in, your browser is given a private key that lets you change or delete it later. My server only stores a hash of this key. If you sign in on that browser later, these presets move under your account.</p>
    <p>Unsharing a preset hides it from everyone else. Deleting a preset removes it from my server.</p>

    <h2>Votes, downloads, and limits</h2>
    <p>I store a salted hash of your IP address. It stops the same person voting on a preset or counting a download more than once, and limits how many presets can be shared each day. Your IP address itself is never stored.</p>
    <p>When you are signed in, votes and the daily share limit use a salted hash of your account id instead.</p>

    <h2>Submissions</h2>
    <p>Submissions can be sent from the website, where you need to be signed in, or as a pull request on GitHub. The Blockbench plugin cannot send them. A submission sent from the website stores the file you send, its name, the credit, any notes and settings you give it, its review status, and which account sent it.</p>
    <p>Submissions are public. Each one is opened as a pull request on the title generator's public <a href="https://github.com/ewanhowell5195/MinecraftTitleGenerator" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub repository</a>, which shows the file, its name, the credit, your notes, your username, and whether you use Discord or GitHub. Anyone with the link can also see the submission's page on the title generator.</p>
    <p>Withdrawing a submission removes it from my server and closes its pull request, but the pull request stays on GitHub, and I can still accept it. If a submission is accepted, it becomes part of the title generator, and the credit is shown on the <a href="/credits/">credits page</a>.</p>
    <p>You and reviewers can comment on your submission, on its page or on its pull request. Comments are public and are kept on the pull request on GitHub, not on my server. Comments written on the site are posted there with your username, and the submission's page shows them from there.</p>
    <p>When someone comments on your submission, or it is accepted or turned down, a notification is saved to your account. This stores their username, their comment, and a link to it. Reviewers are also notified when you send, change or comment on a submission, which shows them your username.</p>
    <p>Each notification is also emailed to you, with the same details. Sending a submission needs an email address on your Discord or GitHub account for this.</p>

    <h2>Usage stats</h2>
    <p>When you render, save, or share a title, the title generator sends a list of the fonts, textures, and overlays it uses to my server. This is used to show the most popular ones first, and to count how many titles have been made.</p>
    <p>It does not include your title's text, your account, or any fonts or images you have added yourself.</p>

    <h2>Stored in your browser</h2>
    <p>The title generator saves these in your browser, or in Blockbench when you use the plugin, and they do not leave your device unless described above:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Your current title, including any images and fonts you have added to it.</li>
      <li>Your saved presets and view settings.</li>
      <li>Your work in the font editor.</li>
      <li>Your votes, downloads, the presets you have shared and their keys, and your account's username and profile picture link, so the title generator can remember them.</li>
      <li>Recently loaded preset pages, so they load faster.</li>
      <li>Minecraft files the title generator has downloaded from Mojang, so they do not need downloading again.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Clearing your browser's site data, or the plugin's data in Blockbench, removes all of these. Keys for presets you shared without signing in cannot be recovered, so you will not be able to change or delete those presets afterwards.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>The title generator only uses two cookies, and both are needed for signing in:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>session</strong> keeps you signed in. It lasts 90 days, or until you sign out.</li>
      <li><strong>signin_state</strong> protects the sign in from being tampered with. It lasts 10 minutes, and is removed once you are signed in.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>There are no tracking, analytics, or advertising cookies.</p>

    <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your account id and username are kept until you delete your account, or until you have no presets or submissions left.</li>
      <li>Presets under your account and shared presets are kept until you delete them.</li>
      <li>Vote and download records are kept until the preset is deleted. Changing a shared preset's title resets them. Your own votes are deleted when you delete your account.</li>
      <li>Daily share counts are deleted after the day ends.</li>
      <li>Submissions are removed from my server once they are accepted, turned down or withdrawn, along with their notifications. When one is accepted or turned down, you are left one notification saying so, which is kept until you clear it. Deleting your account removes all of your notifications.</li>
      <li>Your email address is removed from my server once you have no submissions waiting for review, unless you are a reviewer.</li>
      <li>Deleted data can remain in Cloudflare's database history for up to 30 days.</li>
      <li>Resend keeps a copy of each notification email for 30 days after it is sent.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>I never sell your data. It is only shared with the following services, to run the title generator:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare</a></strong> hosts the title generator and its database. Every request to the title generator goes through Cloudflare, including your IP address.</li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://discord.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discord</a></strong> and <strong><a href="https://github.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></strong> handle signing in, and show your profile picture.</li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://www.blockbench.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Blockbench</a></strong> runs the plugin.</li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://github.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></strong> hosts submissions as public pull requests, as described above.</li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://resend.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Resend</a></strong> sends notification emails, so it receives your email address and each notification.</li>
      <li><strong><a href="https://www.mojang.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Mojang</a></strong>: when you use a Minecraft block texture, your browser downloads the game's files directly from Mojang's servers.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These services have their own privacy policies, and any data they collect is not governed by this policy. Links to other websites are not covered by this policy either.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>I am responsible for the data described in this policy, and can be contacted through the contacts listed below.</p>
    <p>Data is processed on the basis of legitimate interests: providing the features you choose to use, showing shared presets and submissions, and preventing abuse of the title generator.</p>
    <p>You have the right to access, correct, export, and request the removal of your data, and to object to or restrict how it is processed, except where this policy states otherwise. To use these rights, contact me through the contacts listed below.</p>
    <p>If you are unhappy with how your data is handled, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (<a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>).</p>

    <h2>Removing your data</h2>
    <p>To delete your account, use the <a href="/account/">Manage account</a> page. This always deletes the presets saved to your account, your votes, and your notifications. To keep a copy of your presets, download them first.</p>
    <p>You then choose what happens to your shared presets and submissions. They can stay without your username, and your shared presets keep their votes and ratings. Or they can be removed: your shared presets are deleted, and your submissions are removed from my server, and withdrawn if they are waiting for review.</p>
    <p>Signing out removes the session cookie, but does not delete anything from my server.</p>
    <p>To remove anything else, contact me through the contacts listed below.</p>
    <p>Some data cannot be removed on request:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Accepted submissions stay in the title generator, under the submission terms in the <a href="https://github.com/ewanhowell5195/MinecraftTitleGenerator/blob/main/LICENSE.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">licence</a>.</li>
      <li>Pull requests and their comments cannot be deleted from GitHub. Deleting your account removes your username from them, and I can remove your notes on request.</li>
      <li>Deleted data can remain in Cloudflare's database history for up to 30 days.</li>
      <li>Notification emails already sent stay with Resend for 30 days after they are sent.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
    <p>Discord and GitHub do not provide accounts to children under the age of 13, so signing in to the title generator is not for children under 13 either. Everything else can be used without an account. If you are a parent or guardian and you are aware that your child has given me personal data, please contact me so that I can remove it.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>If you have any questions about this policy, you can contact me:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>On Discord: <a href="https://discord.ewanhowell.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ewan's Server</a></li>
      <li>By email: <a href="mailto:contact@ewanhowell.com">contact@ewanhowell.com</a></li>
      <li>On GitHub: <a href="https://github.com/ewanhowell5195/MinecraftTitleGenerator/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open an issue</a></li>
    </ul>
  </main>
